/// Behavioral API documentation for the Roadie Roster backend.
/// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source; reads no state.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Roadie Roster Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nBackend for **Roadie Roster**, the new-hire tracking app for Bubba's 33 store #975 in Lake Charles, LA (opening Mon Feb 8, 2027). It stores store configuration, positions (stations) with build-to targets, the opening schedule, checklists, retention settings, roadie cards, kiosk sign-up submissions, access grants, the admin-set kiosk PIN, and the phase-2/3 records (orientation check-off, attendance, training groups, trainer notes, leader talks, final sign-offs, alerts).\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method that reads or writes application data requires a **signed (non-anonymous) caller**. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nSigning in is not enough: a principal must be **registered** before any role-guarded call succeeds. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend and calls `requestAccess()` once. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\nA **direct API caller** (an agent that never loads the frontend) must first call `_initialize_access_control()` once as a signed-in caller. The platform's shared authorization assigns the role by whether the caller is the first initializer:\n\n- `first_caller_role` — the **first** initializer of `_initialize_access_control()` becomes `#admin` in the shared authorization state (the shared authorization owner).\n- `later_caller_role` — every **later** initializer becomes `#user` in the shared authorization state.\n\nThis platform role is separate from the app's own access grant: the first initializer still needs `bootstrapAdmin()` to bridge that grant into an app Admin, and later initializers still need an Admin to approve them with `approveUser()` before any role-guarded call succeeds.\n\n- `requestAccess()` records the caller in the pending list and returns `true` when the caller is already registered (or already pending). It is safe to call repeatedly.\n- An unregistered or anonymous caller receives a trap on every guarded endpoint: `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- A Kiosk login receives `Access denied: Kiosk logins may only submit a sign-up` on every read.\n- An expired access grant (past its access end date) is treated as unregistered.\n\n### Registration evidence\n\nThe access model has exactly two registration rows, decided by whether the caller is the platform's first authenticated user:\n\n| Row | Caller | Role assigned |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `first_caller_role` | The platform's first authenticated user (the shared authorization owner) | `admin`, via `bootstrapAdmin()` while no app admin exists yet |\n| `later_caller_role` | Any later (non-first) initializer who signs in and calls `requestAccess()` | none yet — the caller is recorded as a **pending** request with no role and stays pending until an Admin approves them with `approveUser()` |\n\n- **First caller.** The platform's shared authorization mixin makes the first authenticated principal an admin of the shared authorization state. `bootstrapAdmin()` bridges that grant into the app: it succeeds only while no app admin exists yet and only for that first principal, and it returns `true` when the caller holds an app Admin grant after the call. A later caller calling `bootstrapAdmin()` gets `false` and no grant, because an app admin already exists. `adminCount()` reports the number of non-expired admins.\n- **Later callers.** Every other signed-in principal starts with no role. `requestAccess()` records them in the pending list and returns `false` on the first call, `true` when they are already registered or already pending; it is idempotent and safe to call repeatedly. A pending caller may submit a staff profile with `submitStaffProfile(profile)` and read their own request with `getMyPendingRequest()`, but every role-guarded endpoint still traps until an Admin approves them.\n- **Approval.** `approveUser(request)` (real Admin only) removes the pending entry and creates the caller's access grant with the requested role, trainer stations, linked roadie and staff profile. An Admin grant is always stored with no end date. Until then, `getMyAccess()` returns a `null` grant and the frontend keeps showing the waiting screen.\n\n### First-admin bootstrap\n\n`bootstrapAdmin()` bridges the platform's shared authorization grant into the app's access model. It succeeds only while no app admin exists and only for the platform's first user; it returns `true` when the caller holds an app Admin grant after the call. `adminCount()` reports the number of non-expired admins.\n\n## Roles and authorization\n\nRoles: `admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `leadership`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `kiosk`, `integration`.\n\n- **Admin** — full access; the only role that may manage access grants, store configuration, positions, schedule, checklists, retention, and the kiosk PIN.\n- **Store Manager** — manager-level access: roadie cards with contact sets, sign-up approval, build-to adjustment, trainer notes, exports.\n- **Trainer** — sees every roadie card (name, photo and card fields) regardless of stations; contact-set fields stay hidden. Trainer notes stay narrower: a trainer reads notes only for roadies in their approved stations.\n- **Integration** — sees only the Shareable export; every roadie card, change-log entry, and trainer-note read returns nothing.\n- **Kiosk** — may only submit a sign-up; every read traps.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **Timestamps** are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (matching `Time.now()`).\n- **Date-only** values are UTC-midnight nanosecond timestamps; exactly zero means \"not set\". A negative value is a real pre-1970 date and is handled correctly by the age helpers.\n- **Identifiers** (`RoadieId`, `PositionId`, `EventId`, `CrewId`, `SignupId`, `ChangeLogId`, `TrainingGroupId`, `LeaderTalkId`, `AlertId`) are `Nat`.\n- **PhotoRef** and **SignatureRef** are platform file-storage references (blob bytes), not text. Fetch a roadie photo with `getPhoto(id)` and a sign-up photo with `getSignupPhoto(id)`; both return `null` when absent or not visible.\n- **Availability** is a list of `{ day, shift }` cells; `day` is one of `wed..tue` and `shift` is `am` or `pm`.\n- **isMinor** and **birthdayMonthDay** are non-sensitive derived values recomputed on every read from the contact-set date of birth in the store time zone, so a roadie who turns 18 stops being flagged as a minor on the next read. `birthdayMonthDay` is `\"MM-DD\"` or `null`.
- **hireDate** is an optional `Timestamp` (nanoseconds) on every roadie card: the day the roadie submitted their kiosk profile. `approveSignup` sets it from the sign-up's `submittedAt`. Existing roadies migrated from before this field fall back to the matching sign-up's `submittedAt` when it can be found, otherwise to the approval time recorded in `hiredAt`; the migration never leaves it `null`. It is returned by `listRoadies`, `getRoadie`, and `listRosterForPosition` (it is not a contact-set field, so it is not redacted). Render it in the store time zone.\n\n## Store configuration and logos\n\n- `getStoreInfo()` (any read-capable role) returns the full store configuration, including `logo` and `secondaryLogo`, each an optional `PhotoRef` (`null` when unset).\n- `getStoreLogo()` is a **public query with no role gate**: any caller, including Kiosk logins and unregistered or anonymous principals, may call it. It returns `{ logo, secondaryLogo }` — both optional `PhotoRef` values — so the kiosk and sign-in screens can render the store logos without passing `getStoreInfo`\'s role gate. An absent logo is `null`.\n- `updateStoreInfo(info)` (Admin only) replaces the whole store configuration, so it persists both `logo` and `secondaryLogo`; pass the current values to keep a logo unchanged.\n\n## Uniforms\n\n- `getUniformSettings()` (Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager) returns `{ sizeCurve, bufferPercent }`. `sizeCurve` is `{ shirts : [{ size, percent }], hats : [{ size, percent }] }` where each `percent` is a whole percentage; each set is intended to total 100 but is saved with a warning, never blocked. `bufferPercent` is the order buffer (default 10).\n- `updateUniformSettings(settings)` (Admin or Store Manager only, logged) replaces the whole uniform settings value. It is refused while demo mode is on with `Turn off demo mode to change real settings`.\n- `getUniformOrder(filter)` (Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager) returns `{ filter, bufferPercent, rows, sizeUnknown }` for `filter` of `#all`, `#foh` or `#boh`. Each `rows` entry is `{ item, size, hired, projected, orderTotal }`: `hired` counts Pending + Active roadies (archived excluded) using their real shirt/hat sizes and their position's uniform defaults; `projected` splits each position's unfilled build-to slots by the size curve and multiplies by that position's defaults; `orderTotal` is `(hired + projected)` with the buffer added and rounded up. `sizeUnknown` lists roadies missing a shirt or hat size as `{ roadieId, name, missingShirt, missingHat }` so the page can link to their card. Demo records count only while demo mode is on.\n- Per-position uniform defaults (`shirtType`, `shirtQty`, `hatType`, `hatQty`) are edited on the position and travel in the store template; `shirtQty`/`hatQty` accept 0.\n- Roadie shirt and hat sizes live on the roadie profile (`shirtSize`, `hatSize`); they are not contact information and are visible to leaders.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `getMyAccess()` returns the caller's own access view `{ grant : ?AccessGrant; demoRole : ?DemoRole }`. `grant` is the caller's **real** access grant, or `null` until an Admin approves them; the frontend polls it while showing the waiting screen and treats a `null` grant as \"still waiting\", not an error. `demoRole` is the caller's own impersonated demo role while demo mode is on, or `null` when demo mode is off. The two are deliberately separate: a caller with no real grant is never presented as really approved just because demo mode is on.\n- `getMyPendingRequest()` is a read-only query that returns the caller's own pending access request, derived from the message caller (never an argument). It returns `null` when the caller has no entry in the pending list, otherwise `{ requestedAt, hasProfile }`: `requestedAt` is the nanosecond `Timestamp` when the caller registered, and `hasProfile` is `true` once the caller has submitted a staff profile on that pending request. The approval gate uses it so a pending user who already submitted a profile goes straight to the waiting screen after a reload. It never mutates state.\n- `listPendingSignups()` returns only `#pending` submissions and never includes photo bytes.\n- `getRosterSummary()` returns per-position `{ positionId, positionName, onHand, buildTo, openSpots }`; on-hand counts each roadie once under their main position only.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `requestAccess()` is idempotent.\n- `approveSignup(id, ...)` traps when the submission has already been decided; a retry after success is rejected rather than creating a second roadie.\n- `approveUser(request)` traps when the principal has no pending request; it removes the pending entry on success.\n- `archiveRoadie` requires a reason; `rehireRoadie` requires a non-blank reason. `updateRoadieStatus` can never set or clear `#archived`.\n- `updateAccessEnd` refuses **any** end date (past or future) on an admin grant, and an Admin grant is always stored with no end date. `updateUserRole` and `removeUser` refuse to leave zero active admins.\n- `adjustBuildTo` applies a signed delta to the stored build-to targets and records a `BuildToAdjustment`.\n\n## Kiosk PIN\n\n- `setKioskPin(pin)` (Admin only) stores only a one-way hash of the PIN; the plaintext is never persisted or returned. An empty PIN traps.\n- `checkKioskPin(pin)` returns `true` when the candidate matches the stored hash; it is a query callable by any caller so the kiosk can gate entry.\n- `hasKioskPin()` returns `true` once an Admin has set a PIN.\n\n## Exports\n\n- `buildShareableExport()` (any read-capable role) returns the export with **no** contact set and **empty** availability arrays, so it never leaks availability.\n- `buildFullExport()` (Admin/Store Manager only) fills the whole contact set, availability by shift and by day, and records a `buildFullExport` change-log entry.\n- Both fill the overview totals: `fohTotalPar`/`bohTotalPar`/`grandTotalPar` and the matching `*Need` fields.\n\n## Errors and traps\n\n- Unregistered or expired callers trap with `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- Missing role traps name the required role, e.g. `Access denied: Admin role required`.\n- Missing records trap with a message such as `Roadie not found` or `Position not found`.\n- A roadie below a position's minimum age traps on `approveSignup` and `changePosition`.\n\n## Profile fields (About Me)\n\nEvery roadie card and sign-up carries a `RoadieProfile`. The free-text About Me fields are all optional `?Text` and are capped at 200 characters on submission (`submitSignup`): `preferredName`, `hometown`, `hobbies`, `favoriteMovie`, `favoriteSnack`, `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteDrink`, `favoriteColor`, `funFact`, `goalHere`, `positionAppliedFor`. `shirtSize` and `hatSize` are also `?Text` and capped at 200 characters.\n\n- `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteDrink` and `favoriteColor` are the three Gift Bag fields. They were added to `RoadieProfile` by migration `00000006_000000.mo`, which defaults them to `null` for every existing roadie and sign-up so no prior answer is lost. Managers may edit them through `updateRoadieDetails`.\n- `favoriteMovie` is retained on the stored record so existing answers are preserved, even though the kiosk form no longer collects it.\n\n## Gift Bags\n\n- `getGiftBags(filter)` is a **query** returning the Gift Bags shopping list and printable labels. `filter` is `#all`, `#roadies`, `#leaders`, `#foh`, `#boh`, or `#position(PositionId)`. `#all` selects every active (non-archived) roadie plus every leader; `#roadies` selects active roadies only; `#leaders` selects leaders only; `#foh`/`#boh` select roadies by the house of their main position; `#position` selects roadies by main position id.\n- **Leaders** are the manager, trainer and leadership roles (`admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `leadership`) taken from the access grants. A leader's label carries their title in `positionName` (falling back to a role label), their name, and their About Me answers; leaders have no roadie id (it is `0`) and no house (it is `#foh`).\n- **Authorization:** Admin, Store Manager and Training Manager only. Every other caller — including Kiosk, Trainer, Leadership, Visiting Manager, Integration, unregistered and anonymous principals — is rejected with `Access denied: Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager role required`.\n- The payload never includes phone, email, date of birth or any other contact-set field.\n- `groups` holds one `GiftBagGroup` per category (`#candySnack`, `#drink`, `#sportsTeam`, `#color`, `#shirtSize`, `#hatSize`). Each group's `answers` are grouped **case-insensitively, ignoring extra spaces and punctuation** (for example `snickers`, `Snickers!` and `  SNICKERS ` are one group), the `answer` shown is the most common spelling in the group, and the list is sorted by `count` highest first. `noAnswer` counts selected roadies who left that category blank or unanswered.\n- `labels` holds one `GiftBagLabel` per selected roadie: `roadieId`, `name`, `positionName`, `house`, and the six answers (`candySnack`, `drink`, `sportsTeam`, `color`, `shirtSize`, `hatSize`), each optional. Labels carry no contact information.\n\n## Export columns\n\nBoth the Full and Shareable exports include the four Gift Bag columns `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteSnack`, `favoriteDrink` and `favoriteColor` on every `ExportRow`, populated from the roadie's profile. They are not contact information, so the Shareable export includes them too. The Full export additionally fills the contact-set columns (phone, email, emergency contact, date of birth, availability).\n\n## Staff profiles\n\nA signed-in user may supply a **staff profile** describing who they are. It is stored on their pending request before approval and carried onto their access grant at approval.\n\n- `submitStaffProfile(profile)` (any signed-in caller with a pending request) stores the caller's profile on their pending request. It traps with `No pending request for this principal` when the caller has no pending request (for example an already-approved user). Calling it again replaces the stored profile.\n- `updateMyStaffProfile(profile)` (any signed-in caller with an access grant) updates the caller's own profile on their grant. It traps with `Access grant not found` when the caller has no grant. Existing users approved before profiles existed use this to fill theirs in without losing access.\n- `approveUser(request)` carries `request.staffProfile` onto the new grant; pass the pending request's profile to preserve it.\n- A `StaffProfile` carries `fullName`, `requestedRole`, `title`, `homeStoreNumber`, `homeStoreCity` (all required), and optional `preferredName`, `workPhone`, `workEmail`, `photo`, `trainerPositionIds`, `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`. `arrivalDate`/`departureDate` are `DateOnly` (UTC-midnight nanoseconds); `photo` is an optional `PhotoRef`.\n- The optional About Me fields `hometown`, `hobbies`, `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteSnack`, `favoriteDrink`, `favoriteColor`, `funFact`, `goalHere`, `shirtSize` and `hatSize` were added to `StaffProfile` by migration `00000008_000000.mo`, which defaults them to `null` for every existing grant and pending request. A blank field is stored as absent (`null`).\n- Work phone and email are contact information: only Admin and Store Manager may read them, matching the roadie contact-set rule. `listLeaders` clears both before returning a leader's profile.\n\n## Leaders\n\n- `listLeaders()` is a **query** returning one `LeaderSummary` per leader: `principal`, `role`, `title`, `staffProfile`, `trainerPositionIds`, `arrivalDate` and `departureDate`. Leaders are the manager, trainer and leadership roles (`admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `leadership`).\n- **Authorization:** readable by every registered role except Kiosk and Integration. Kiosk is rejected with `Access denied: Kiosk logins may only submit a sign-up`; Integration is rejected with `Access denied: Integration role may only read the Shareable export`; unregistered and anonymous principals are rejected with `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- `title` is the leader's staff-profile title, falling back to a role label (`Admin`, `Store Manager`, `Training Manager`, `Visiting Manager`, `NSO Trainer`, `Leadership`) when the profile is absent or its title is blank.\n- The returned `staffProfile` has `workPhone` and `workEmail` cleared, so no contact information ever leaves the backend. Leaders never count toward on-hand or build-to and never appear in the position roster.\n\n## Crews\n\nA **crew** is a manager's team. Every crew has an **owner** (`leaderPrincipal`), the approved manager who leads it. A crew created through `createCrew` always has an owner; crews created before owners existed may still have `leaderPrincipal = null` and keep working (the UI shows \"No manager yet\" with a \"Pick manager\" button).\n\n- `listCrews()` (query) returns every crew as `{ id, name, leaderPrincipal, isDemo }`. `leaderPrincipal` is the approved manager who owns the crew, or `null` when the crew has no owner yet. Readable by every registered role except Kiosk and Integration.\n- `listCrewSummaries()` (query) returns every crew as `{ id, name, leaderPrincipal, roadieCount, isDemo }` for the kiosk approval Crew dropdown. `roadieCount` is the number of **pending + active** roadies assigned to the crew; **archived roadies are excluded**. Readable by every registered role except Kiosk and Integration.\n- `createCrew(name, leaderPrincipal)` (Admin or Store Manager only) creates a crew owned by `leaderPrincipal` and returns the new `CrewId`. The owner is **required** and must be an approved **Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager** leader; an NSO Trainer, Visiting Manager or Leadership principal is rejected. A manager may own **only one** crew: creating a second crew for the same owner traps `<Name> already has a crew`. A crew created while demo mode is on is a demo crew.\n- `updateCrew(id, name, leaderPrincipal)` (Admin or Store Manager only) renames a crew and/or changes its owner. Pass `null` to clear the owner. A new owner must be an eligible manager (Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager) and may own only one crew. Traps with `Crew not found` for an unknown id.\n- `deleteCrew(id)` (Admin or Store Manager only) removes a crew. It refuses while any roadie is assigned to the crew, trapping with `Move its roadies first.`; reassign those roadies before deleting.\n- `getMyCrew()` (query) returns the caller's **own** crew for the Today screen: the crew they own and one row per roadie assigned to it (photo, name, position, Pending/Active, paperwork \"x of y\", and red tags for \"Absent today\" and \"Paperwork overdue\"). It returns `null` when the caller owns no crew. Any read-capable role may call it.\n- Every crew create, rename, owner change and delete is recorded in the change log with a detail string naming the crew.\n- **Authorization:** all crew writes require Admin or Store Manager; a caller without that role is rejected with `Access denied: Admin or Store Manager role required`.\n- **Demo manager picker:** while demo mode is on and the caller's demo role is Store Manager or Training Manager, `setDemoManagerAs(managerPrincipal)` chooses which demo manager the caller views as, so `getMyCrew` and the Roster \"My crew\" chip match that manager's crew. The choice is stored per caller and defaults to the first demo manager; it is used **only** for crew-ownership matching and is ignored outside demo mode. See the Demo mode section.\n\n## Duplicate matches\n\n- `findDuplicates(id)` (Admin or Store Manager only) returns the roadie cards that share the submission's phone number or email, including archived roadies. Each `DuplicateMatch` is `{ roadieId, name, mainPositionName, matchedOn, archived }`.\n- `name` is the matched roadie's display name (preferred name when set, otherwise the full name); `mainPositionName` is their main position's name (empty when the position is unknown); `matchedOn` is `\"phone\"`, `\"email\"` or `\"both\"`; `archived` is `true` when the matched roadie is archived. The UI names the roadie and links to their card; `roadieId` is never shown raw.\n\n## Store templates\n\n- `downloadStoreTemplate()` (Admin only) returns a `StoreTemplateFile` built from the current positions, schedule, checklists and leader-talk settings. Schedule events are expressed as whole days relative to the store's opening date (`startOffsetDays`, optional `endOffsetDays`; negative = before opening). The file carries a `version` number and deliberately no people data, logos, store number, city or opening date.\n- `loadStoreTemplate(file)` (Admin only) validates and applies a template. It returns `#err(text)` when any roadie exists (`Cannot load a template once roadies exist`); otherwise it replaces positions, schedule and checklists, recomputes every schedule date from this store's opening date, updates the leader-talk name and sizes, and returns `#ok(preview)` with the applied counts. Position and event ids are reassigned sequentially from zero.\n- `saveStoreTemplate(name)` (Admin only) snapshots the current configuration under a name in the in-canister template store; it is separate from the downloadable file.\n\n## Mutation retry safety (continued)\n\n- `submitStaffProfile` and `updateMyStaffProfile` are idempotent replacements: re-sending the same profile is safe.\n- `loadStoreTemplate` is destructive: it clears and replaces positions, schedule and checklists. Re-running it with the same file is safe (it refuses once roadies exist, and otherwise reproduces the same state).\n\n## Demo mode\n\nDemo mode lets an Admin rehearse the whole app against fake data without touching real records. It is **off by default** and every demo record is separated from real records by an `isDemo` flag on each record (roadies, sign-ups, crews, attendance/check-ins, trainer notes and change-log entries).\n\n### Turning it on and off\n\n- `getDemoState()` is a **public query with no role gate**: any caller, including unregistered or anonymous principals, may call it, so the sticky banner can render on the sign-in and waiting screens. It returns a `DemoStateView` with `enabled`, `turnedOnAt`, `autoOffAt`, `pretendDate`, `demoRole`, `demoTrainerStations`, `demoTrainerAs` and `demoManagerAs`. `demoRole` and `demoTrainerStations` describe the **requesting caller's own** demo role, or `null`/empty when demo mode is off or the caller is anonymous. `demoTrainerAs` is the demo leader the caller views as (defaulting to the first demo leader who leads a group), and `demoManagerAs` is the demo manager the caller views as (defaulting to the first demo manager); both are `null` when demo mode is off.\n- `setDemoMode(enabled, confirmation)` requires a **real Admin grant** (an impersonated demo role is ignored). Turning it **on** requires the literal confirmation text `DEMO`; any other value is rejected. Turning it on sets `autoOffAt` to eight hours after the switch-on time, and the backend turns demo mode off automatically once that time passes. Turning it on while it is already on is refused (`Demo mode is already on`), so the eight-hour window cannot be extended. Turning it off clears the pretend date and **every** caller's stored demo role. Every on/off is written to the change log.\n- `setDemoRole(role, stations)` (any signed-in caller, demo mode only) sets the **calling principal's own** impersonated demo role and, for a demo NSO Trainer, the station ids that role may see. The choice is stored per caller, so one person's \"View as\" choice never changes anyone else's view. An anonymous caller is refused (`Sign in to choose a demo role`).\n- `setDemoTrainerAs(trainerPrincipal)` (any signed-in caller, demo mode only) chooses which demo leader a demo NSO Trainer views as, so \"View as NSO Trainer\" can see that leader's group. It rejects a principal that is not a demo group leader with `Pick a demo trainer`.\n- `setDemoManagerAs(managerPrincipal)` (any signed-in caller, demo mode only) chooses which demo manager a demo Store Manager or Training Manager views as, so `getMyCrew` and the Roster \"My crew\" chip match that manager's crew. It rejects a principal that is not a demo manager. The choice is stored per caller and used **only** for crew-ownership matching; it is ignored outside demo mode.\n- `setPretendDate(pretendDate)` (any signed-in caller, demo mode only) sets or clears the pretend \"now\". `null` restores the real clock. `pretendDate` is `{ day : DateOnly; shift : #am | #pm }`.\n\n### The demo data firewall\n\nWhile demo mode is **on**, every query and export returns **only** demo records; real roadies, contact info, leaders and exports are never visible or changeable. While demo mode is **off**, demo records are invisible everywhere and never count toward on-hand, build-to, exports, gift bags or the store template. The separation is enforced in the backend, not the UI.\n\n### Impersonated demo role\n\nWhile demo mode is on, any **signed-in** caller — even an unapproved one — acts as their own chosen demo role against demo data only. A signed-in caller who has not chosen a role defaults to demo Admin. An **anonymous** caller always gets no role, even while demo mode is on, so every role check (admin, manager, kiosk, readable, registered) treats an anonymous caller as unregistered. The backend enforces the **same permission rules** for the impersonated role as for a real user with that role, so a demo Trainer still cannot see contact info. The demo role is one of `#admin`, `#storeManager`, `#trainingManager`, `#trainer`, `#visitingManager`, `#leadership`, `#kiosk`.\n\n### Real-data guard\n\nEvery write that changes real, shared settings requires a **real** Admin (or, for build-to, a real Admin or Store Manager) grant and is refused while demo mode is on, trapping with `Turn off demo mode to change real settings`. This applies to `approveUser`, `updateUserRole`, `removeUser`, `updateAccessEnd`, `updateTrainerStations`, `setKioskPin`, `updateStoreInfo`, `createPosition`, `updatePosition`, `deletePosition`, `createScheduleEvent`, `updateScheduleEvent`, `deleteScheduleEvent`, `updateChecklists`, `updateRetentionSettings`, `adjustBuildTo`, `saveStoreTemplate`, `loadStoreTemplate` and `downloadStoreTemplate`. Reading positions, schedule and store info stays allowed while demo mode is on, because the demo needs them.\n\n### Demo-scoped access listings\n\n- `listAccessGrants()` (Admin only) returns only demo leaders while demo mode is on, and only real grants while it is off; real grants are never exposed in demo mode.\n- `listPendingUsers()` (Admin only) returns only demo pending requests while demo mode is on, and only real pending requests while it is off.\n- `getMyAccess()` returns the caller's **real** grant unchanged (or `null` when they hold none) plus a separate `demoRole` field carrying the caller's own demo role while demo mode is on, or `null` when demo mode is off. A caller with no real grant is therefore never presented as really approved.\n\n### Pretend date\n\nWhile demo mode is on, the pretend date overrides \"now\" for schedule windows, countdowns, the Today screen, check-in availability and age math, so Orientation day, Training Days 1-4, Friends & Family and opening week can be rehearsed. The pretend date is shown in the banner.\n\n### Demo data\n\n- `getDemoDataSummary()` counts the demo records currently loaded (roadies, sign-ups, crews, attendance, trainer notes).\n- `loadDemoData()` (Admin, demo mode only) seeds the demo data set: about 40 roadies across positions with illustrated avatars and full About Me answers, a mix of statuses, 2 minors and 2 archived; 6 manager-owned crews (\"<First>'s Crew\", one per demo manager); 6 demo Store Managers (home store 975, Platinum card) plus Renee Hollier (Market Partner) and 2 NSO Trainers (Kristen Marcotte, Ramon Delgado); and 3 pending kiosk sign-ups, one a duplicate by phone. Every non-archived demo roadie is assigned to a crew: back-of-house positions round-robin across the three Kitchen Manager crews, front-of-house positions round-robin across the three Service Manager crews.\n- `clearDemoData()` (Admin, demo mode only) removes every demo record, including demo orientation check-offs, final sign-offs, training groups and leader talks. Real records are never touched.\n- In demo mode, kiosk sign-ups are saved as demo sign-ups.\n\n## Orientation, rosters and paperwork\n\n### Roster state (pending vs active)\n\nEvery roadie carries `rosterState`, either `#pending` (hired, not yet shown up) or `#active` (marked Present at an orientation session). `approveSignup` creates the roadie as `#pending` and assigns the next upcoming orientation session automatically when the manager did not pick one. On-hand and build-to counts include both pending and active roadies; archived roadies are excluded from every count. `getRosterSummary()` returns per-position `onHand`, `pending`, `active`, `buildTo` and `openSpots`; `getDashboard()` returns the store-wide `hired`, `active`, `pending`, `buildToTotal`, `stillNeeded`, `showedAtOrientation` and `certified` totals plus the FOH/BOH position lists.\n\n### Orientation sessions\n\nOrientation sessions are schedule events of kind `#orientation`. The store seeds a single default session (\"Orientation · Sat Jan 30, 2027, 9:00 AM\"); an Admin may add a second session or a makeup session through the schedule endpoints. `approveSignup` assigns the next upcoming session; `moveRoadieToSession(roadieId, eventId)` (Admin/Store Manager) moves a roadie to another session.\n\n#### Session assignment\n\n- `listOrientationSessions()` (Admin, Store Manager, Training Manager, Visiting Manager) returns every `#orientation` schedule event as `{ eventId, name, start, end }`, ordered by `start` ascending. `start` and `end` are nanosecond `Timestamp`s; `end` is optional. Use it to populate a session picker.\n- `listUnassignedPendingRoadies()` (same roles) returns the pending roadies with no usable session: `orientationEventId` is `null`, or points to an event that is missing from the schedule or is not an `#orientation` event. Each row is `{ roadieId, name, photo, positionId, positionName, crewId, crewName }`. Archived roadies are excluded. A roadie whose assignment points at a deleted or non-orientation event appears here even though their stored `orientationEventId` is non-null.\n- `moveAllRoadiesToSession(fromEventId, toEventId)` (Admin/Store Manager only, logged) moves **every non-archived roadie** currently assigned to `fromEventId` to `toEventId` and returns the number moved. It is the bulk counterpart to `moveRoadieToSession`, used to merge two sessions before deleting the emptied one. The target must be an existing `#orientation` event or the call traps `Schedule event is not an orientation session` (or `Orientation session not found` when the id is absent). The source need not exist. It is **not idempotent in the sense of a no-op**: calling it again after the move returns `0` because no roadie remains assigned to the source. It does not touch attendance records, so a roadie already marked Present at the source keeps that attendance row; delete the emptied source only after confirming no attendance references it.\n\n### Orientation check-in screen\n\n- `getOrientationSessionView(eventId)` (Admin, Store Manager, Training Manager, Visiting Manager) returns the session's assigned roadies with photo, name, position, crew and paperwork status, plus `presentCount` / `assignedCount`. A roadie is `noShow` once the session's date has passed while they are still pending and assigned to that session.\n- `markPresent(roadieId, eventId)` (Admin/Store Manager) is **idempotent**: several managers may call it concurrently and the result converges. It sets the roadie's `rosterState` to `#active` and records attendance. Poll the session view (for example every 10 seconds) to pick up other managers' marks.\n- `undoPresent(roadieId, eventId)` (Admin/Store Manager, logged) returns the roadie to `#pending` and clears the attendance record for that session.\n- `archiveNoShows(eventId)` (Admin/Store Manager) archives every roadie still pending and assigned to a session whose date has passed, with reason `#ncnsOrientation`. It traps when the session has not passed yet. Returns the archived roadie ids.\n- `rehireRoadie(id, reason)` (Admin/Store Manager) requires a non-blank reason, returns the roadie to `#pending` and assigns the next upcoming orientation session; the rehire is logged with who and the reason.\n\n### Paperwork gate\n\nThe schedule's `#deadline` event (\"Paperwork due\") is the single source of the paperwork due date; `StoreInfo` no longer carries a separate date. It is the date by which every roadie's paperwork must be complete. A roadie's paperwork is complete when every paperwork checklist item that applies to them is checked, respecting `requiresAlcoholCert` (\"Only alcohol positions\") and `minorOnly` (\"Only under 18\"). After the due date, incomplete roadies are flagged. Store managers tick paperwork items through `updateOrientationCheckoff`.\n\n### Uniform check-off\n\n- `getUniformCheckoff(roadieId)` (Admin/Store Manager) returns the uniform items from the orientation uniform checklist, each with its `itemType` (`#checkbox` or `#count`), plus `locked`, `complete` and `missing`. It is **locked** (read-only) until the roadie's paperwork is 100% complete. Shirt and hat count items pre-fill from the position's `defaultShirts` / `defaultHats`.\n- `saveUniformCheckoff(checkoff)` (Admin/Store Manager) traps with `Paperwork incomplete` while the roadie's paperwork is not complete.\n\n### Demo partitioning\n\nOrientation check-offs, final sign-offs, training groups and leader talks each carry `isDemo`. Every read, list and update filters on `isDemo == demoActive`, and a write to the other partition is rejected. `clearDemoData()` removes demo orientation check-offs, final sign-offs, training groups and leader talks along with the other demo records.\n\n## Training group boards (shift boards)\n\nA **shift board** is the training-group plan for one shift: a `#trainingDay` or `#friendsAndFamily` schedule event plus an `#am` or `#pm` shift. Friends & Family events have a single `#pm` shift only. A board is keyed by `eventId` and `shift`; the key is the text `\"real:<eventId>:am\"` (or `\"demo:<eventId>:am\"` for a demo board), so a demo board and a real board for the same event and shift never collide.\n\nA board holds `groups` (one entry per trainer: `trainerPrincipal`, `capacity`, `roadieIds`) and `offRoadieIds` (roadies marked Off this shift). **A roadie may appear in at most one group, or in Off, per shift**; the backend rejects a board that places the same roadie twice with the trap `A roadie may appear in at most one group or in Off`. Default capacity comes from the Admin `trainingGroupSize` setting (default 4); a Training Manager may change it per trainer per shift.\n\n### Reading boards\n\n- `getShiftBoard(eventId, shift)` (every read role except Kiosk and Integration) returns the board view or `null` when no board exists for that shift. The view carries `groups` (each with its trainer, `capacity` and roadie chips), `unassigned` (active roadies not in a group or Off for this shift) and `offThisShift`. Each roadie chip carries `roadieId`, `name`, `photo`, `positionId`, `positionCode` and `markedUnavailable`.\n- `listShiftBoards()` (every read role except Kiosk and Integration) returns every board in the current partition, ordered by event id then shift.\n- `markedUnavailable` is `true` when the roadie is scheduled on a shift they marked unavailable on the kiosk. Availability is by weekday and shift; a roadie with no availability recorded is treated as available.\n- Demo boards are visible only while demo mode is on; while it is off, demo boards are invisible.\n\n### Editing boards\n\nAll board writes require **Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager** (`requireGroupEditor`). While demo mode is on, a **real** board write is additionally refused with `Turn off demo mode to change real settings`; demo boards stay editable in demo mode. Every board write is recorded in the change log.\n\n- `saveShiftBoard(board)` replaces one shift's groups, capacities and Off list. It rejects a duplicate placement (see above), validates every roadie id (must exist, be in the active partition and not be archived) and every trainer principal (must hold an Admin, Store Manager, Training Manager, Trainer or Visiting Manager grant; in demo mode a demo leader is accepted), and stamps `editedAt`.\n- `copyShiftBoard(eventId, shift, fromEventId, fromShift)` copies the source shift's groups, capacities and Off list onto the target shift, replacing the target board. It traps `Source shift board not found` when the source is missing or belongs to the other partition.\n- `autoFillShiftBoard(eventId, shift)` fills each group's empty capacity from the Unassigned pool, dealing candidates round-robin across the groups that still have open capacity so no group is filled to capacity before the next gets a roadie. A same-station pass (roadies whose main position matches the trainer's stations) runs first, then an any-candidate pass. Only roadies available that shift are used, and already-placed roadies are never moved.\n- `clearShiftBoard(eventId, shift)` empties the shift's groups and Off list.\n\n### Group-change notices\n\nWhen a board edit adds or removes roadies in a trainer's group for a **current or future** shift, the backend stores a per-trainer notice carrying the shift label, the added and removed roadie names and the editor's name.\n\n- `listGroupChangeNotices()` returns the caller's own undismissed notices, newest first. Any read-capable role may call it; it returns only notices addressed to the caller.\n- `dismissGroupChangeNotice(id)` marks one of the caller's own notices dismissed. It traps `Group change notice not found` for a notice that is not the caller's or belongs to the other partition.\n- Notices carry `isDemo` and follow the demo partition.\n\n### My group\n\n- `getMyGroup()` returns the signed-in caller's own group for the current or next shift (the earliest board on which they train a group), with the shift label, capacity and their roadies' name, photo and position code. It returns `null` when the caller trains no group. Any read-capable role may call it.\n\n## Trainer check-in\n\nA check-in record is keyed by shift (event id + AM/PM) and roadie, one record per roadie per shift, upserted. Each record carries `state` (`#present`, `#late` or `#absent`), an optional `lateAt` timestamp, an optional `excused` reason, `recordedBy`, `recordedAt` and `isDemo`. Records are partitioned by the demo flag, so a demo check-in and a real check-in for the same shift and roadie never collide.\n\n### Shift window and the trainer lock\n\nA shift's start and end are the event's date plus the store's AM or PM shift start and end times in the store time zone; a Friends & Family night uses the PM times. A trainer may create or change records from **30 minutes before the shift start until 2 hours after the shift end**, computed on the effective clock (the demo pretend date while demo mode is on). Outside that window only Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager may change records, and those changes are logged. A trainer outside the window receives the trap `Check-in is locked; ask a manager to change`.\n\n### Permissions\n\n- Admin, Store Manager and Training Manager may check in anyone on a shift.\n- A trainer may check in only roadies in their own group on that shift's board. Any other roadie traps `Access denied: you may check in only roadies in your own group`.\n- Visiting Manager and Leadership are read only.\n\n### Endpoints\n\n- `recordCheckIn(eventId, shift, roadieId, state, lateAt, excused)` upserts one roadie's check-in for a shift. Marking a roadie `#absent` raises an absent alert; changing them off absent archives it. Every write is logged. It traps `Roadie is archived; rehire first` for an archived roadie and `Shift not found` for an unknown event.\n- `getCheckInBoard(eventId, shift)` returns the caller's own group on that shift as a check-in board: a row per roadie with photo, name and current state, plus `checkedInCount` / `totalCount` and a `locked` flag that is true when the caller may no longer edit. It returns `null` when the caller has no group on that shift's board. Any read-capable role may call it.\n- `listAbsentAlerts()` returns the unarchived absent alerts for Admin, Store Manager and Training Manager, newest first. `phone` is present only when the caller may see the roadie's contact set (Admin and Store Manager), so Call/Text is never rendered for other roles. Demo alerts are visible only while demo mode is on.\n- `excuseAbsentAlert(id, reason)` excuses an absent roadie with a short reason (Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager). The reason is required and traps `An excuse reason is required` when blank; the record stays but is not counted as unexcused.\n- `archiveAbsentAlert(id)` archives an absent alert (Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager).\n- `moveAbsentRoadieToOtherShift(id)` moves an absent roadie to the same day's other shift, into that shift's Unassigned tray (Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager). The other shift's board is created when missing.\n\n## Today\n\n- `getToday()` returns the Today page payload shaped by the caller's role: `role`, `myGroup` and `checkIn` for a trainer, `absentAlerts` for Admin/Store Manager/Training Manager, `shiftSummaries` (per-shift present/late/absent counts) for Admin/Store Manager/Training Manager/Leadership/Visiting Manager, and `nextEvent` (the next upcoming event with `startsInMs`) when no shift is today. Any read-capable role may call it.\n";
  };
};
